From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:05:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201: add the PERIC0 sysreg and
 pin controller

Add the PERIC0 system registers and the PERIC0 pin controller with its
GPIO banks gpp0-gpp19, as in Google's gs201 device tree. The PERIC0 USI
blocks select their mode through the sysreg, and the camera modules'
I2C buses, master clocks and resets, the camera PMIC's bus and several
other peripherals sit on PERIC0 pins.

The pin controller stays disabled here; boards that use PERIC0 pins
enable it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-pinctrl.dtsi | 143 ++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi  |  21 +++
 2 files changed, 164 insertions(+)

